# Test: a single-hop BFD peer written with an IPv6 zone is refused.
#
# VALIDATES: `ze config validate` refuses `single-hop-session fe80::b%zbl0`,
#            naming the leaf and its value and saying to write the link in
#            `interface` (AC-7 of spec-bfd-link-local-peer-zone).
# PREVENTS: the link spelled twice, in the zone and in `interface`, where the
#           two can disagree.

stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
bfd {
    enabled true;
    bind-v6 true;
    single-hop-session fe80::b%zbl0 {
        interface zbl0;
    }
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=bfd: single-hop-session fe80::b%zbl0: peer "fe80::b%zbl0" carries a zone: write the address as fe80::b and the link in interface
